    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: First-Time Visitors Traffic Preparation</h1>
    <p>Hanoi traffic is the part of a motorbike rental that no brochure can prepare you for and no rider should meet unprepared. The city's streets run on a continuous, negotiated flow that rewards calm and punishes both timidity and bravado, and first-time visitors who prepare for it deliberately, with the right mindset, the right habits and a sensible progression, consistently ride better by day three than they believed possible on day one. This guide is that preparation, at first-rental speed.</p>
    <p>This page belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> series for first-time visitors and stays on traffic preparation. The rules of the road, helmets, licensing and the rest of the legal frame, are covered cautiously on the <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/hanoi-motorbike-traffic-rules/">Hanoi traffic rules guide</a>; the verified prices for every machine are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, and the general rental questions live on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">The mindset: reading the river</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">Before you ride: helmet, machine and route</a></li>
